  "schematicNotes": [
    {
      "id": "n_heavy",
      "text": "HEAVY DC: trunk battery -> cabin PDB (glove box, ST185-EngineRoom-C) -> RADLOK 5.7 mm through the firewall -> starter B+. 160 A alt B+ joins the starter post and does not recross; its protection is NOT at the starter (see n_alt_prot). Jump lugs at trunk battery, PDB, starter, engine block, and the engine-bay jump post. 2 AWG is OK for cranking; 160 A continuous charge may need 1/0 + 8 mm RADLOK - see the table. Moved out of ST185-EngineRoom-C into its own file 2026-10-11 (harness-reconcile pass, Section 40.1 step 4) - the cabin PDB (and everything it also feeds: cabin fuse block, glove-box body block, OEM hot, AM1/AM2) stays on EngineRoom-C; only the H1-H8 heavy-DC chain moved.",
      "width": 390,
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 1710,
        "y": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n_alt_prot",
      "text": "ALTERNATOR OUTPUT PROTECTION (Daniel 2026-09-28): a fusible link or an inline fuse / breaker on the positive cable at the trunk battery or near the cabin fuse box / PDB - never at the starter post. Size for the 160 A alternator (plan 6.20: 175 A). Battery is AGM.\nKILL SWITCH (Dan 2026-10-13, J2; DECISIONS S21 / R64): Longacre 52-45780 in the trunk (175 A main, 20 A alternator pole). Main pole: battery + -> MAIN 1, MAIN 2 (LOAD) -> H1 -> PDB BAT+ -> PDB ALT/STR -> H3 -> RADLOK -> starter B+, where the alternator B+ (w_alt) lands - so the alternator is on the LOAD side. Second pole: the alternator IG (excite, J/B No.1 ECU-IG 15A via IG2-15, 16 AWG for the 15 A fuse) runs glove box -> RH sill (with H1 / H2) -> ALT 1 / ALT 2 -> back -> RH fender grommet -> G2-3. Switch off = battery cut AND excite cut, so the alternator cannot keep the engine running; the G4X Stop Switch input stays as well (R19).\nSPIKE PROTECTION (info only, not drawn): opening the main pole while the alternator charges can load-dump into the loads. Option: a cutoff with alternator protection (Pegasus 4430 re-routes the alternator output to ground) - Daniel's call, not part of this build.",
      "width": 390,
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 1710,
        "y": 330
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "shdr_1",
      "text": "FIREWALL RADLOK",
      "width": 270,
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 1710,
        "y": 960
      },
      "color": "Orange"
    },
    {
      "id": "n_rev4",
      "text": "ROUTE 1 REV 4 (Dan's mark-up, 2026-10-10): battery box moved to the passenger-side rear corner of the trunk (H1/H2 rerouted from there - bundle lengths above are inherited estimates from the prior ST185-EngineRoom-C drawing, not re-measured against the new spot - verify on the car). Starter moved to Dan's spot (lower-middle of the engine, p.29 leaders S2/S3). H4 (RADLOK+ -> starter) and H5 (alt B+ -> starter) now run as one bundle along the firewall and down to the starter (Dan: \"run 1 and 3 together\") - drawn as separate conductors here (H4 via RADLOK/rl_pos_eng, H5 via t_alt_b/w_alt) since harness.design has no native \"co-routed, not bundled-as-one-cable\" primitive; the physical bundling is a routing note, not a schema change. Alternator moved to the rear of the engine, RH side, under bulkheads A/B (MR2-style, rev 3 Dan mark-up 2026-10-04). The G2 round 3-pin plug (alt_plug, Toyota 90980-10341) is drawn here (Dan 2026-10-13, R17); its IG / L / S leads break off to ST185-EngineRoom-C and cross the firewall in harness C's own RH fender grommet (no ECU signal, so no bulkhead letter, R2) - IG and L to the cowl-side IG2-15 / IG2-16 leads under the ECU, S to the glove-box RFRM ALTS 2A.",
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 1710,
        "y": 1080
      },
      "width": 390
    }
  ],
